nk:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(249.222931 117.665263) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" d=\"M 3501 0 L 563 0 L 563 474 L 1811 474 L 1811 4070 L 1766 4070 L 640 3021 L 326 3360 L 1510 4467 L 2349 4467 L 2349 474 L 3501 474 L 3501 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(331.988482 124.056842) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3b\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p032bd3d8bc\"><rect x=\"43.148281\" y=\"11.528\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 2 · Increase in store costs this year ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Wages ($0.95M) and energy ($0.50M) explain 85% of the increase. The wage rise is driven by the legal minimum wage, so it won't reverse.</p> <p>To earn $5.4M again at today's $9 per basket and $15.2M of store costs, Meadowlane needs ($5.4M + $15.2M) ÷ $9 = <b>2.29M baskets</b>, 15% more than today and more than it ever had.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> volume alone won't fix this. Meadowlane needs to win back some baskets <i>and</i> run its stores more efficiently.</p>"},{"q":"What would you recommend to the owners?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p><b>Win back shoppers near the discounter</b></p><ul><li>Price-match 100 everyday staples; keep margin on fresh, local and deli</li> <li>A loyalty scheme so Meadowlane knows who has stopped coming</li></ul> <p><b>Lower store costs</b></p><ul><li>Self-checkouts and staff rotas matched to footfall by hour</li> <li>Energy: LED lighting and doors on fridges (often a 1 to 2 year payback)</li></ul> <p><b>Find out first:</b> is the basket loss all at the store near the discounter? If so, it's a local problem, not a brand problem.</p>"}],"reco":"Profit halved because store costs rose $1.7M (mostly wages and energy) and Meadowlane lost 5% of its baskets after a discounter opened; supplier inflation was passed on in full, so it isn't the cause. Volume alone can't fix it: getting back to $5.4M would need 15% more baskets. I recommend price-matching everyday staples at the affected store, plus self-checkouts, footfall-based rotas and an energy programme. Risk: price-matching erodes margin if it spreads beyond staples. Next step: check basket trends store by store.","great":["Builds a bridge instead of listing causes","Notices price and cost of goods cancel out","Turns 'win back volume' into a number and sees it isn't enough","Asks whether the loss is local to one store"],"id":23,"slug":"meadowlane-grocers"}